    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created, the response now includes `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names. Two changes, each in its natural home:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field (it's an output-only derived value, so it lives on `Owner`, not the editable `OwnerFields`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `displayName` via a small `displayName(Owner)` default method (`lastName + \", \" + firstName`, null-guarded). The DTO boundary is the right place to compute a derived response field, and keeping it in one helper method avoids bloating the responder functions.\n\nBoth the `POST /api/owners` responder and `GET /api/owners/{id}` responder go through `toOwnerDto`, so the field is populated consistently. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` passes and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
